1. She is anemic and has to take iron tablets. (Verbatim: "I'm anemic by the way. Um, and I have to take iron tablets.")
2. She finds iron tablets unpleasant to take because they taste like metal. (Verbatim: "They taste like metal. They literally taste like metal. It's like licking metal.")
3. She has difficulty swallowing pills and always needs water to take them. (Verbatim: "I can't have it without water... I still can't do it without water though.")
4. As a child, she refused to take tablets and disliked dissolved medications due to their awful taste. (Verbatim: "When I was a kid I refused to have like tablets and then they would try like dissolved versions... they taste awful.")
5. She used to have to take a lot of medicine as a child. (Verbatim: "I used to have, I don't have as many now, but my goodness... I've had lots of medicines.")
6. She overcame her fear of choking on pills by realizing she had accidentally swallowed small candies like gummy bears and Skittles without choking. (Verbatim: "I accidentally swallowed a gummy bear and thought wait I didn't unalive... I won't choke it'll be okay.")
7. She had a temporary model before her official debut, which is common among independent VTubers. (Verbatim: "Some VTubers do... independent VTubers will do this because it takes a while and it takes a lot of money to get a proper model.")
8. It took her a couple of months to get her proper model after starting to stream. (Verbatim: "It took for me it took a couple of months okay.")
9. She loves streaming so much that she couldn't wait to start, even before her debut model was ready. (Verbatim: "I really love streaming... I couldn't not stream like it's my being.")
10. She acknowledges that debuting with an expensive model without prior streaming doesn’t make financial sense for most people. (Verbatim: "It doesn't make much sense to just eat tons of money at an expensive model without ever streaming before right.") [end of text]



1. Elia chose to become a VTuber instead of pursuing a career in medicine. (Verbatim: "i'm really happy you picked this career over the medical stuff... i feel like i wouldn't be in a very good state of mind if i pursued it")

2. Elia identifies as a zombie, not a vampire. (Verbatim: "remember that ellie is not a vampire she's a zombie zombie zombie")

3. Elia has a calmer alternate persona named Elenoir. (Verbatim: "we also have elenoir... sleepy and calm elia gives me nice cozy feeling")

4. Elia has a history of growing up around horrible people, which made her view of humanity difficult. (Verbatim: "it's hard to believe when you get the unfortunate childhood of growing up around horrible people")

5. Elia believes there are wonderful people in the world despite past hardships. (Verbatim: "i can also also also also also confirm that there are some really wonderful people out there")

6. Elia expresses a desire to be cute and has tried searching online for how to be cute. (Verbatim: "i wish i was cute i wish i was i do wish but i've googled how to be cute and and it didn't it it didn't get anywhere")

7. Elia values self-care and prioritizing mental and physical health. (Verbatim: "rule number one is take care of yourself... put yourself first don't donate if you can't... prioritize putting your sleep first")

8. Elia has a loud stomach that often makes embarrassing noises. (Verbatim: "my stomach has always had an issue with being quite loud and just making noises")

9. Elia prefers her current model over her previous one because it allows more expressiveness. (Verbatim: "this model is here to stay... i enjoy being able to be more expressive like i enjoy my face being free")

10. Elia hopes to brighten people’s days and bring light during dark times. (Verbatim: "i hope i can make it a little brighter because you know when you get in that state sometimes it does feel like i don't know") [end of text]



1. She wants to make people happy and sees it as a core goal of her streaming. (Verbatim: "i want to try and make people happy like like you know i it is a goal of mine")

2. She is concerned about losing early supporters if she grows in popularity. (Verbatim: "i was really scared well i'm still scared that if if i do grow that some of you will leave")

3. She remembers regular chat members' names and appreciates their return after absences. (Verbatim: "i do remember names that i see regularly and i remember seeing names that come back after being gone for a while and it does make me smile")

4. She values all donation sizes equally and feels obligated to acknowledge every one. (Verbatim: "i want to read all the donuts no matter how small because i know it can be a lot for some people")

5. She has strong memory for recurring chat members despite admitting difficulty with other types of recall. (Verbatim: "i'm not good at remembering faces i'm not good at left some rights i'm not good at maps... but i remember you guys okay")

6. She is determined and stubborn, rejecting the idea of impossibility when faced with challenges. (Verbatim: "i don't like the idea of things being impossible... i like a challenge")

7. She would use slow chat to maintain readability if chat volume becomes unmanageable. (Verbatim: "if it gets to a point where i struggle to read every message in chat i would put slow chat on so i can read it")

8. She has a playful fictional trait of having "goose wings," though she denies it jokingly. (Verbatim: "elia confirmed her wings are goose wings")

9. She mentions having gone through school exams that required extensive memorization. (Verbatim: "i'm finally using my big memory brain that was trained throughout all of school with those stupid exams")

10. She appreciates being supported during her growth and refers to early fans as part of her journey. (Verbatim: "a bunch of you have been here for pre-debut some of you have found me post-debut like i appreciate it") [end of text]



1. She has a strong affection for stationery and enjoys using themed notebooks and pens. (Verbatim: "I have a lot of notebooks. I really like stationery. I love stationery. I love stationery. It's so good.")
2. She owns and uses a Chainsaw Man-themed notebook and pen. (Verbatim: "What was interesting there is I wrote it in a chainsaw man themed notebook with a chainsaw man themed pen.")
3. She places importance on skincare and takes care of her skin. (Verbatim: "I do look after my skin. Because I am very much into skincare.")
4. One of her goals is to make lots of people happy. (Verbatim: "want to support your dream of making lots of people happy if I at all can.")
5. She is planning to debut a new character named Elenoir (or Eleanor) at the end of the month. (Verbatim: "I think I'm planning for the end of this month.")
6. She is open and direct about expressing her emotions when upset or annoyed. (Verbatim: "If I get upset or annoyed, I very much tell you guys nice and bluntly.")
7. She has a habit of forgetting things but tries to compensate by writing them down. (Verbatim: "I write it down. I write it down. I forgot.")
8. She enjoys making or receiving cat impressions. (Verbatim: "Oh you want a cat impression?")
9. She appreciates fan submissions, such as drawings or "faces of Elia," and was grateful for the response. (Verbatim: "Thank you so much for submitting faces of Elia. I do appreciate that a ton.")
10. She likes chicken burgers and mentions them as a desirable meal. (Verbatim: "Eat a yummy chicken burger.") [end of text]



1. She started her VTubing journey using a free model called Omoeri, which she used for Omori streams. (Verbatim: "this is omoeri that i used for my omori streams")

2. Before obtaining her current custom model, she used a temporary model purchased from Nizima for $60. (Verbatim: "this is the model that i got from nizima for um is it like 60 buckaroos")

3. Her current model cost thousands of dollars, with more money spent on rigging than on the artwork. (Verbatim: "this one was thousands um so yeah that's that's kind of the different levels of investment" and "i actually spent um more on the rigging more in the rigging than the art")

4. She invested extra in advanced facial rigging using V Bridger, which allows for detailed expressions like nose movement, cheek puffing, and tongue tracking. (Verbatim: "V Bridger means I get more mouth shapes... my nose actually moves my nose moves my cheeks there's like very subtle cheek movements")

5. She used a simple PNG image with an open mouth as an early form of her avatar before using rigged models. (Verbatim: "you can actually start with just a picture with an open mouth picture... this is another form actually")

6. She taught herself how to use YouTube Studio, OBS, and other streaming tools independently. (Verbatim: "i had to teach myself how to use youtube studio i had to teach myself how to use obs teach myself basically taught myself how to do all the stuff")

7. She has no experience with 3D models and admits her knowledge in 3D is extremely minimal. (Verbatim: "honestly my my um knowledge in 3d is extremely minimal i've never ventured into 3d")

8. She believes people should not be restricted from VTubing due to financial limitations and supports starting with free or low-cost options. (Verbatim: "i don't like the idea of people being restricted by financial financial things")

9. She had a pre-debut phase and considers her official debut to have occurred later than when she first started streaming. (Verbatim: "that's why i had this pre-debut" and "that's why I have a debut that's a bit later than actually when I started streaming")

10. She jokes about being short, referencing her chibi form and sitting with knees up. (Verbatim: "hey not because i'm short or anything though" and "i sit with like my knees up") [end of text]



1. She used to work as a developer before becoming a VTuber. (Verbatim: "i worked as a developer um got myself in a more stable position before i started vtubing")

2. She chose not to pursue a PhD due to financial struggles and lack of passion, opting instead for VTubing. (Verbatim: "i very very this this this sentence like stuck in my mind was when my professor was like you can't just do a phd because you want the fancy title and i was like um oh but that is that is that is exactly why i i i want to do the phd")

3. Her primary motivation for considering a PhD was the desire for the title and her parents' approval, not genuine academic passion. (Verbatim: "that is definitely the primary reason why um yeah that is the reason that is the reason that is that is that is the i wanted the fancy title i wanted the bragging rights of it and i wanted my parents to be like yay because that's what they wanted")

4. She comes from a family that equated success with traditional academic achievements like earning a PhD. (Verbatim: "i would not pursue a phd um i only ever did all of that because my parents taught me that that was the only way to be successful at life")

5. She has a dog that chewed and cracked her old Huawei phone when it was a puppy. (Verbatim: "my dog was a puppy and she she she decided to nom it and it's cracked it's cracked on the on the front")

6. She prefers to keep old phones as backups and doesn’t like changing phones often. (Verbatim: "when i get a phone i'm one to keep it for as long as i can um actually i still like you know i still keep those phones as backup phones")

7. She currently uses an iPhone 13 for facial tracking in her VTubing setup. (Verbatim: "i don't use the latest iphone though um i use a iphone 13")

8. She believes iPhone facial tracking is the best available despite the high cost. (Verbatim: "the iphone is definitely the um peak of um facial tracking as as annoying as and upsetting as that is to say because iphones are hiking expensive")

9. She went through a prolonged period of existential crisis when deciding between a PhD and VTubing, staying up late and deeply reflecting on her goals. (Verbatim: "gosh it was taking months of existential crises um it was my it was this it was my ek guy graph not mine but you know")

10. She values authenticity and emotional connection, aiming to create a “cringe place” where people can be unapologetically themselves. (Verbatim: "sometimes it feels like um i don't know that yeah the only cool places to be are usually places that are edgy and kind of mean... and i feel like that's what the world needs the world needs a cringe place and i make that cringe place") [end of text]



1. Her childhood nickname was "Mama Elia." (Verbatim: "mama elia was trying to say something to me")
2. Her parents had high expectations for her academic and financial success, pressuring her to attend Oxford or Cambridge and secure a high-earning job. (Verbatim: "you need to do well at school you need to go to oxford or cambridge when you're older you need to be very very very successful")
3. As a child, she prioritized playing with Legos over listening to her parents’ expectations. (Verbatim: "i was looking behind her thinking i just want to play with the legos behind you")
4. She once believed her life purpose was to earn money for her family due to parental pressure. (Verbatim: "being a small child i fully believed that that was like my purpose was to be raised and earn them money")
5. She pursued VTubing as the first endeavor where she considered what she personally wanted in life. (Verbatim: "going into vtubing was the first time that i thought what what do i what do i want like like what what do i actually want to do")
6. She completed a master’s degree in AI and previously worked as a developer. (Verbatim: "i got my first it job um before my master's degree in ai" and "i went into ai")
7. She delayed pursuing her own goals due to fear of failure and financial responsibilities to her family. (Verbatim: "i was scared... i wasn't in a financial position to take those risks either because you know family needed money")
8. Her educational and career path was highly varied, including drama, music, sciences, medicine, biochemistry, animal biology, IT, and graphic design. (Verbatim: "my path is a complete mess because i did like um what you call it like um drama and music in secondary school and then i did like sciences... and then i went into ai")
9. She considered multiple career paths such as musical theater, acting, journalism, media, and directing, but felt held back by systemic barriers like connections being more important than talent. (Verbatim: "i wanted to do musical theater acting journalist... it felt unfair because it was like who you knew not how good you were")
10. She finds VTubing uniquely fulfilling because it combines all her varied interests and talents into one pursuit. (Verbatim: "vtubing combines it all for me it combines all the things that i love together so much") [end of text]



1. VTubing combines her diverse interests including technology, entertainment, journalism, and music, fulfilling a long-standing desire to integrate her passions. (Verbatim: "vtubing brings together like there is a tech aspect there is like um what you call it like you know entertainment aspect there's there is technically a journalistic aspect to it there's music aspect there's it just combines all these things that i absolutely like have always enjoyed and wanted to put together")

2. She felt very alone growing up and wishes VTubers had existed during her youth to provide comfort. (Verbatim: "i felt very alone a lot of the time growing up and i wish vtubers were a thing back then")

3. One of her core motivations for being a VTuber is to be there for others who feel isolated, inspired by her younger self. (Verbatim: "i'm just trying to be you know there for past me i guess")

4. Her purpose in content creation is to make people happy and feel connected. (Verbatim: "the final piece that was missing was just like the feeling like i have a purpose um yeah and and and that is like the purpose right there that to try and make people happy")

5. She is British. (Verbatim: "i'm british sorry um for anyone wondering")

6. She owns anime figurines that are displayed on shelves covering her wall. (Verbatim: "my wall isn't available it's filled with shelves that are covered in anime figurines")

7. She prefers to wear shorts underneath her skirt. (Verbatim: "don't worry you won't see my butt because i wear shorts underneath my skirt always")

8. She uses two horizontal monitors, one of which is second-hand and currently glitching. (Verbatim: "can confirm i used two horizontal monitors but recently one of my monitors has been acting a bit funny like it's been like glitching out a bit")

9. She got her second-hand monitor from eBay and is unsure of its age. (Verbatim: "i got it from like i don't know ebay or whatever")

10. She is considering upgrading to a single large monitor due to space and practicality constraints. (Verbatim: "do you think two two big monitors would be better or one long boy monitor") [end of text]



1. She has long hair, which people in school mistook for extensions. (Verbatim: "as you know my hair is quite long so like they'd be like take those hair extensions out and i'd be like it's not hair extension that's just the length of my hair")

2. She keeps her nails at an average length and paints them, but teachers in school used to complain about them. (Verbatim: "i paint them and they're not super long they're not super long they're like average length... the teacher always thinking that i had um like... take those nails off and i'm like they're they're my real nails")

3. Her two go-to hairstyles are a high ponytail and two plaits (braids). (Verbatim: "one is a ponytail and one is two plaits like this")

4. She finds a high ponytail and braids practical, especially in environments like jungles or zoos, to prevent hair from getting caught or grabbed. (Verbatim: "unlike a ponytail a ponytail can get caught really easily... and it's not above me for for a giraffe to grab when i was at the zoo")

5. She is not a vampire. (Verbatim: "i'm not a vampire you punk i'm not a vampire... just to clarify i'm not a vampire")

6. She refers to herself humorously as a "banana chinned oshi." (Verbatim: "this is me your banana chinned oshi")

7. She used to live without Wi-Fi after moving and relied on mobile data. (Verbatim: "I haven't had wi-fi since I moved and I've been watching streams on mobile data")

8. She enjoys s'mores and was thinking about making them. (Verbatim: "I was thinking about marshmallows... I wanted to have s'mores s'mores")

9. She has a habit of drinking Coca-Cola, though she only had one can on her desk during the stream. (Verbatim: "the answer is one... it's because my order of coca-cola didn't arrive yesterday")

10. She drinks a lot of water, keeping four glasses on her desk. (Verbatim: "there's four by the way there's four") [end of text]



1. She was not allowed to have long hair during primary school and had to keep it short, which she disliked. (Verbatim: "the reason why i i very much adore having long hair is because i wasn't allowed long hair growing up um in primary school")

2. She finally gained the freedom to grow her hair long starting in secondary school, and she strongly values this personal choice. (Verbatim: "it wasn't until like secondary school that i was finally permitted to grow my hair out... i just wanted it to be like long")

3. Her hair grows continuously and does not seem to have a natural stopping length, which she believes may be due to genetics. (Verbatim: "mine just mine just keeps going if I don't cut it um yeah it just it just keeps growing")

4. She has long nail beds and does not bite her nails, a habit she never developed despite knowing many who do. (Verbatim: "yeah my nail beds her are quite long um yeah i don't know i'm not one to bite my nails um i've never understood i've never fully gotten into that habit")

5. She had a negative experience during a primary school surfing trip in England, where she got too cold and was removed from the class due to safety concerns. (Verbatim: "i got kicked out of the surfing class because they are worried about me... my lips were really really really purple and they started getting really worried")

6. She gets cold easily, especially in water, and has previously experienced hypothermia-like symptoms during outdoor activities. (Verbatim: "i get cold very well i used to get cold really easily... i used to always um what you call it get purple lips and stuff")

7. She is unable to swim and considers herself a poor candidate for water-based activities like surfing. (Verbatim: "i can't swim i think i would be a terrible i've tried surfing once")

8. She feels self-conscious about wearing bikinis and would prefer a one-piece swimsuit, possibly with a hoodie for comfort, though she worries it might make her look like a child. (Verbatim: "i'm a bit self-conscious um if i was to wear a bikini but i think i think a bikini with like a hoodie where i could just hide under the hoodie would be fine")

9. Haircuts in England are very expensive for her, with her last cut costing around 60 pounds, which she compares to the price of her pre-debut model. (Verbatim: "my last haircut cost me like um... 60 quid 60 buckaroos it's basically the price of this this this pre-debut model")

10. She reads viewer comments regularly but chooses not to respond or like them to avoid making others feel left out. (Verbatim: "I do read comments that are left um I don't respond or like them typically because I don't want anyone to feel left out but I do read them") [end of text]



1. She was a good student in school and rarely got into trouble. (Verbatim: "you know i was a really good student so i never have oh i remember um i was almost in trouble...")

